sdl3-mixer-timidity
===================

This crate is a modified version of TiMidity: a translation into Rust of
the copy of TiMidity 0.2i ("Experimental MIDI to WAVE converter",
Copyright (C) 1995 Tuukka Toivonen <toivonen@clinet.fi>; the SoundFont
support Copyright (C) 1996,1997 Takashi Iwai) that is bundled with
SDL_mixer 3.3.0 (src/timidity/ at SDL_mixer revision
df66ae893c91b0f6fa5d026a195bb278213d007d, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer),
as stripped and modified there for SDL_sound and SDL_mixer.

It is NOT the original TiMidity, nor SDL_mixer's copy of it.

How and when it was changed: on 2026-10-07, every C source and header file
of that copy that SDL_mixer builds (common, instrum, mix, options, output,
playmidi, readmidi, readsbk, resample, sndfont, tables, timidity, sbk.h,
sflayer.h) was translated, function by function, into the Rust source
files in src/, which keep the original copyright notices and comments.
Each file says so in a line under its copyright notice. The translation
works on Rust types (vectors and references rather than pointers and
linked lists), replaces the global state's C statics with Rust statics
behind locks, and does something defined where corrupt input makes the
C code read or write out of bounds, divide by zero or loop forever (the
places marked "FIXME (upstream)" in the source). Otherwise it renders
bit-for-bit what the C code does, which its tests check. The changes are
freely available as part of https://github.com/danielpclark/SDL.

