TiMidity is licensed under the terms of the Perl Artistic License or the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1, at your choice: see
COPYING (TiMidity's own statement of its terms, verbatim from SDL_mixer),
COPYING.artistic and COPYING.LGPL (both verbatim from SDL_mixer). So is
this crate: its SPDX license expression is
"Artistic-1.0-Perl OR LGPL-2.1-only". (COPYING.LGPL is version 2.1, and
COPYING does not offer a later version.)

This is the only part of the repository that isn't under the zlib
license. sdl3-mixer uses it to play MIDI through its `timidity` Cargo
feature, which is on by default; build sdl3-mixer with
`default-features = false` to leave it (and MIDI) out.

No instrument patches, SoundFonts or timidity.cfg files are bundled. The
test data in testdata/ (small synthetic GUS patches, a SoundFont, MIDI
files and configuration files) is generated by
tools/gen_timidity_testdata.py in the repository.
